cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "UForm: Hardware-Accelerated Distributed Training of Multi-Modal Perception Models across NVLink Domains"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/unum-cloud/UForm
url: https://github.com/unum-cloud/UForm
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.8204323
abstract: >-
  UForm is a family of perception models trained from scratch to share one
  representation across text, images, audio, video, and code, from a single GPU to a DGX node or a
  whole cluster. It builds its training stack bottom-up: distributed primitives that scale
  contrastive learning across nodes, custom NVLink multicast collectives in place of generic
  all-reduce, and GPU data loaders pipelined with the linear-algebra kernels, so decoding never
  stalls the math. Encoders produce embeddings from 64 to 1024 dimensions and serve on CPUs, NVIDIA
  and AMD GPUs, and WebAssembly, behind one C ABI with C++, Python, Rust, JavaScript, and Swift
  bindings.
keywords:
  - distributed training
  - multimodal learning
  - contrastive learning
  - representation learning
  - nvlink
  - gpu
  - quantization

